   I have FORTUNATELY been using this spoiler to deal with Demonlords and
not get hurt at all.  I am sure I am not the first to do this, but here goes
anyway

It's a good one, though


   You will need: (1) Rustproof weapon (depending on the Demonlord)
                  (2) Ring of Conflict
                  (3) Device of Create Monster
                  (4) Some luck

   First, if you are facing a Demonlord alone, you can create a monster that
will keep the Demonlord busy.  Usually, this will reguire a tough creature,
since Demonlords are nasty (no kidding).  This is a case where I like to
have my RoC sitting pretty on my pinky.
   Summon the monster and let the Demonlord and the monster fight it out.
   While they are fighting, start to tear into the Demonlord.
   If you are lucky, the Demonlord will be toast before it has a chance to
come after you.

   My story ... I was feeling rather nasty after coming across a dead 
Priestess, laying dead on her altar.  Hmmmm, I think.  SACRIFICE !!  Well,
Jubilex appeared next to me.  My little kitty didn't like Jubilex too much
and started in on it.  Jubilex kept spitting out my kitty (at least 20
times) ... I KNOW I would NOT survive that sort of beating.  Anyways, this
kept old Jubey busy, while I tore it apart with my rustproof Stormy.
Three rounds later it Jubey was pushin' up the daisies.  I was completely
in tact, armour not damaged and a better Barbarian for the experience.

